urce":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a000b545e52e5880bcecba2cb73de0816618e88adb3a67606beb6921b24548ce","file":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b745181660e1f12343c63ec895c643606fe691635fc5949dc4bad604b759f874","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a000b545e52e5880bcecba2cb73de0816618e88adb3a67606beb6921b24548ce","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nIn ZFC, there exist a countably infinite set $E$ and two infinite matroids\n$M_0,M_1$ on $E$ such that $M_i^*=M_i$ on the same labelled ground set for\n$i=0,1$, and\n\\[\n I_0\\cup I_1\\ne E\n \\quad\\text{for every independent }I_0\\text{ in }M_0\n \\text{ and independent }I_1\\text{ in }M_1.\n\\]\nThe pair $(M_0,M_1)$ has no packing/covering partition. Consequently, the\ninfinite matroid packing/covering conjecture is false."}
